{
  "comprehensible": "The board dealt with the proposal quickly and without much attention, and the CFO was left to take the blame.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "gave the proposal short shrift",
      "gloss": "dealt with the proposal quickly and without giving it much attention or consideration"
    },
    {
      "expression": "carry the can",
      "gloss": "take the blame or responsibility for something that has gone wrong"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "董事会对该提案草草处理，首席财务官只好背黑锅。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "At the last possible moment, he lost his nerve and betrayed his colleagues by blaming them to protect himself.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "bottled it",
      "gloss": "lost his nerve and failed to do something he was expected to do"
    },
    {
      "expression": "threw his colleagues under the bus",
      "gloss": "betrayed his colleagues by blaming them to save himself"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "他在最后一刻临阵退缩，还把同事推出去当替罪羊。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The manager did not admit that the numbers had been changed dishonestly until after the auditors had left.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "doctored",
      "gloss": "changed in a dishonest way to deceive people"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The sentence begins with 'Not until...', which is a negative adverbial. This forces the main clause to use inversion: 'did the manager admit' instead of 'the manager admitted'. The meaning is that the admission happened only after the auditors had gone.",
  "translation": "直到审计员离开之后，经理才承认数据被篡改了。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The house was in a state of dignified but shabby decline, because the people who lived there had moved away to mainland Europe a long time ago.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "genteel decay",
      "gloss": "a condition of being run-down but in a way that still seems respectable or upper-class"
    },
    {
      "expression": "repaired to",
      "gloss": "went to; moved to (a formal or old-fashioned expression)"
    },
    {
      "expression": "the Continent",
      "gloss": "mainland Europe, especially as referred to by British people"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The phrase 'its occupants having long since repaired to the Continent' is a participial clause that gives the reason for the house's condition. It does not have a subject-verb structure like a normal clause; instead, 'having repaired' is a participle phrase meaning 'because they had moved'. The word 'since' here means 'before now', not 'because', which can be confusing.",
  "translation": "这栋房子处于一种体面而破败的状态，因为它的住户早已迁往欧洲大陆。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The results hint at something but do not prove it, and people should not read too much into them.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "suggestive rather than conclusive",
      "gloss": "hinting at a possible answer but not proving it"
    },
    {
      "expression": "ought not to be over-read",
      "gloss": "should not be given more meaning than they actually have"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "这些发现只是提示性的，而非结论性的，因此不应过度解读。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The person renting the property must protect the owner from any claims that come from breaking any of the promises in this agreement.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "indemnify",
      "gloss": "protect someone from loss or damage by paying for it"
    },
    {
      "expression": "lessee",
      "gloss": "the person who rents property"
    },
    {
      "expression": "lessor",
      "gloss": "the person who owns and rents out property"
    },
    {
      "expression": "covenants herein",
      "gloss": "the promises stated in this document"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "承租人应就因违反本协议中的任何承诺而引起的所有索赔，向出租人作出赔偿。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The report does not go as far as to say who is to blame, but the things it suggests are easy to notice.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "stops short of",
      "gloss": "does not go as far as; deliberately does not do something"
    },
    {
      "expression": "apportioning blame",
      "gloss": "saying who is responsible for something bad"
    },
    {
      "expression": "hard to miss",
      "gloss": "very easy to notice or understand"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "报告没有直接归咎于谁，但其中的暗示不难看出。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "He was, to say it in a gentle way, very unhappy with the result.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "to put it mildly",
      "gloss": "used to say that you are describing something in a gentle way, when the real situation is stronger"
    },
    {
      "expression": "not best pleased",
      "gloss": "very annoyed or unhappy"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "说得客气一点，他对这个结果很不高兴。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The committee thought it was just a normal mistake that something had been left out. But actually, it had been left out on purpose, so that the minister would not have to answer a difficult question.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "taken for",
      "gloss": "thought to be; mistaken as"
    },
    {
      "expression": "routine oversight",
      "gloss": "a usual mistake of forgetting something"
    },
    {
      "expression": "deliberate omission",
      "gloss": "something left out on purpose"
    },
    {
      "expression": "spare",
      "gloss": "save from having to deal with"
    },
    {
      "expression": "awkward question",
      "gloss": "a difficult or embarrassing question"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The sentence has a contrast between what seemed true and what was true. The subject is a long clause: 'What the committee had taken for a routine oversight'. This means 'The thing that the committee had thought was a routine oversight'. The main verb is 'was'. The phrase 'designed to spare...' describes the omission and explains its purpose.",
  "translation": "委员会原以为那只是一时疏忽，但实际上那是故意省略的，目的是让部长免于回答一个棘手的问题。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The company was responsible for paying an amount of money that it could not easily pay.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "on the hook for",
      "gloss": "responsible for paying or dealing with something"
    },
    {
      "expression": "a sum it could ill afford",
      "gloss": "an amount of money that it could not easily pay"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "这家公司得为一笔它几乎付不起的款项负责。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "The reaction happens only when a catalyst is there. If there is no catalyst, the activation energy is so high that the reaction cannot take place.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "proceeds",
      "gloss": "happens or goes forward"
    },
    {
      "expression": "in the presence of",
      "gloss": "when something is there"
    },
    {
      "expression": "without which",
      "gloss": "and if it is not there"
    },
    {
      "expression": "prohibitively high",
      "gloss": "so high that it prevents something from happening"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": "The phrase 'without which' introduces a condition that depends on the earlier noun 'catalyst'. It means 'if the catalyst is not present'. The main clause after it describes the result of that condition.",
  "translation": "该反应只有在催化剂存在时才能进行；如果没有催化剂，活化能会高得使反应无法发生。"
}

{
  "comprehensible": "It is proper for us to think about whether this way of acting agrees with what we are obliged to do.",
  "glosses": [
    {
      "expression": "behoves",
      "gloss": "is right or proper for (someone)"
    },
    {
      "expression": "course of action",
      "gloss": "way of doing something; plan"
    },
    {
      "expression": "consonant with",
      "gloss": "in agreement with; consistent with"
    }
  ],
  "grammar": null,
  "translation": "我们应当考虑这样的做法是否符合我们的义务。"
}
